  message: "FIXED, both halves, in the PR merged at dev e6823a6b62.\n\nHALF 1 -- the blanket prefix. `wildcard_imports[0]` was applied unconditionally.\nThe module slot now carries the disjunction the situation actually is: every\nwildcard package PLUS java.lang, comma-joined, reusing the contract cpp has used\nsince INV-funuf (`_module_hint_candidates` asks ANY over disjuncts,\n`module_hint_disjuncts` asks ALL for the coverage gate).\n\nHALF 2 -- the fully-qualified override. `java.nio.file.Files.writeString(...)`\nunder `import java.io.*;` was re-attributed to java.io.Files, because the receiver\narrives as a field_access chain and only its last component survived. A chain\nwhose leading components are lowercase and whose last is capitalised is now read\nas a fully-qualified type and used verbatim.\n\nFIRST STEP ANSWERED, which the item asked for explicitly: the wildcard was\nrecorded as a PREFIX and applied unconditionally, NOT recorded as a candidate and\nmis-ranked. The fully-qualified override is a SECOND, independent bug in the\nreceiver extraction, not the same one -- the item was right to warn they might be\ntwo. The no-import case (whole path in the NAME slot) is a THIRD and is\nINV-januj's defect, fixed separately in PR #684.\n\nTHE FILED REPRO WAS NON-COMPILING JAVA, and the correction matters for the\npopulation figure. `import java.io.*;` + `Files.writeString` does not compile;\nunder a single wildcard the class usually DOES live in that package, so the 1622\nfigure is NOT the affected set. The genuinely broken populations are:\n  - java.lang classes under ANY wildcard -- the dominant case, and not a\n    heuristic: JLS 7.3 makes java.lang.* implicitly imported, so System, String,\n    Integer, Math, Thread are in scope having never been written\n  - files with two or more competing wildcards (464)\n  - fully-qualified call sites\nProvably-wrong population (a java.lang class attributed to a non-java.lang\npackage), measured on real corpus: 170 external refs in jedis ALONE, including\nSystem.currentTimeMillis x28 and System.nanoTime, both catalogued host_info_read.\n\nMEASURED, jedis + spring-petclinic, both arms cold in their own XDG_CACHE_HOME:\n36 boundaries ADDED, 0 REMOVED (removed=0 is the success condition).\n  System.currentTimeMillis x30, nanoTime x4  -> host_info_read\n  System.getProperty x2                      -> env_read (a taint SOURCE)\nALL READ BACK AGAINST SOURCE. MultiDbConnectionProvider.java:567 is a plain\n`System.currentTimeMillis()`. TlsUtil.java:35 is `System.getProperty(\nTRUST_STORE_PROPERTY)` in a file carrying THREE wildcards (javax.net.ssl.*,\njava.io.*, java.security.*) -- the old code picked javax.net.ssl.System and\nmatched nothing, which is the multi-wildcard shape stated as a live instance\nrather than as an argument.\n\nPRECISION GUARD, pinned by test rather than argued: the unqualified class name is\nNOT offered as a candidate. Bare `Files` would match any row whose module ends in\n`.Files`, so a project's own Files class would reach java.nio.file.Files -- the\nINV-dijor shape imported into a recall fix. A repo-local class under a wildcard\nstill matches nothing.\n\nCHECKED AND UNAFFECTED: System.in / System.out travel as module_attr_ref with\nmodule slot `System` and never enter this branch, so PR #684's java ipc_recv fix\nis not disturbed. Java ships zero function-kind rows (139 method, 3 attribute),\nso INV-nizom's multi-candidate `kind != function` filter discards nothing.\n\n9,236 tests pass, 100% coverage on the changed file, mypy ratchet clean.\n\nRESIDUAL: a nested-class reference (Outer.Inner.method()) is correctly NOT read as\na package path, so it still falls through to the wildcard branch and is prefixed.\nPinned by test as current behaviour; a nested type inside a wildcard-imported\nclass is a shape neither half addresses."  # c20b
